High entropy values in .text (137), .rsrc (187), .tvm0 (212), and .reloc (158) indicate compressed, encrypted, or obfuscated content; note that high entropy is a neutral protection signal and not alone indicative of malice (source: verdict calibration). The unusual .tvm0 section (entropy 212, the highest in the file) and large overlay likely contain obfuscated code or embedded payloads.

Malcat's carved file analysis identified 21 embedded files, including 2 PE executables (76KB and 2.7MB), a 606KB ZIP archive, multiple DIB/ICO image files, and an embedded program (source: malcat, carved_files). The virtual file system mapping (source: malcat, virtual_files) reveals the embedded payloads are organized as:
