These imports confirm the sample is capable of process injection, anti-debugging, downloading external payloads, communicating via HTTP, establishing registry persistence, creating new processes, and dynamically resolving APIs to hide its functionality. The sample also includes a manifest requiring administrator execution level (source: ghidra strings), indicating it will request elevated privileges when run, a common trait of malware that requires system-level access for injection or persistence.

